</div><ul class="entry-meta" data-type="simple:slash" data-id="meta_2" ><li class="meta-author"><a class="ct-meta-element-author" href="https://automaton-media.com/en/author/carlos-zotomayor/" title="Posts by Carlos &quot;Zoto&quot; Zotomayor" rel="author"><span>Carlos "Zoto" Zotomayor</span></a></li><li class="meta-date" ><time class="ct-meta-element-date" datetime="2026-06-17T18:32:06+09:00">2026-06-17 18:32</time></li></ul></article><article class="entry-card card-content post-65791 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-news tag-japan-related-news" ><ul class="entry-meta" data-type="simple:slash" data-id="meta_1" ><li class="meta-categories" data-type="simple"><a href="https://automaton-media.com/en/news/" rel="tag" class="ct-term-3">News</a></li></ul><h2 class="entry-title"><a href="https://automaton-media.com/en/news/japanese-live-action-dating-sim-where-you-reincarnate-as-a-pet-hamster-and-get-spoiled-rotten-by-three-sisters-is-finally-coming-back-after-steam-store-page-rem/" rel="bookmark">Japanese live-action dating sim where you reincarnate as a pet hamster and get spoiled rotten by three sisters is finally coming back after Steam store page removal </a></h2><a class="ct-media-container boundless-image" href="https://automaton-media.com/en/news/japanese-live-action-dating-sim-where-you-reincarnate-as-a-pet-hamster-and-get-spoiled-rotten-by-three-sisters-is-finally-coming-back-after-steam-store-page-rem/" aria-label="Japanese live-action dating sim where you reincarnate as a pet hamster and get spoiled rotten by three sisters is finally coming back after Steam store page removal "><img width="768" height="501" src="https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/20260424-65791-001JPG-768x501.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="Sweet Hamster Days " decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/20260424-65791-001JPG-768x501.jpg 768w, https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/20260424-65791-001JPG-380x248.jpg 380w, https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/20260424-65791-001JPG.jpg 1423w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" style="aspect-ratio: 4/3;" /></a><div class="entry-excerpt"><p>Kodansha's Sweet Hamster Days, originally announced in August 2025, is back on track after a temporary Steam removal.</p>
</div><ul class="entry-meta" data-type="simple:slash" data-id="meta_2" ><li class="meta-author"><a class="ct-meta-element-author" href="https://automaton-media.com/en/author/amber-vjestica/" title="Posts by Amber V" rel="author"><span>Amber V</span></a></li><li class="meta-date" ><time class="ct-meta-element-date" datetime="2026-04-25T21:30:00+09:00">2026-04-25 21:30</time></li></ul></article><article class="entry-card card-content post-56082 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-news tag-japan-related-news" ><ul class="entry-meta" data-type="simple:slash" data-id="meta_1" ><li class="meta-categories" data-type="simple"><a href="https://automaton-media.com/en/news/" rel="tag" class="ct-term-3">News</a></li></ul><h2 class="entry-title"><a href="https://automaton-media.com/en/news/japanese-indie-game-in-which-you-use-your-stupid-little-hamster-as-a-war-weapon-of-mass-annihilation-launches-to-very-positive-score-on-steam/" rel="bookmark">Japanese indie game in which you use your stupid little hamster as a war weapon of mass annihilation launches to Very Positive score on Steam</a></h2><a class="ct-media-container boundless-image" href="https://automaton-media.com/en/news/japanese-indie-game-in-which-you-use-your-stupid-little-hamster-as-a-war-weapon-of-mass-annihilation-launches-to-very-positive-score-on-steam/" aria-label="Japanese indie game in which you use your stupid little hamster as a war weapon of mass annihilation launches to Very Positive score on Steam"><img width="768" height="432" src="https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/20260123-56082-header-768x432.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/20260123-56082-header-768x432.jpg 768w, https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/20260123-56082-header-380x214.jpg 380w, https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/20260123-56082-header.jpg 1344w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" style="aspect-ratio: 4/3;" /></a><div class="entry-excerpt"><p>Japanese publisher Kodansha and solo developer Zxima released MOCHI-O on January 19, to a Very Positive Steam review score.</p>
</div><ul class="entry-meta" data-type="simple:slash" data-id="meta_2" ><li class="meta-author"><a class="ct-meta-element-author" href="https://automaton-media.com/en/author/djordje-p/" title="Posts by Đorđe P" rel="author"><span>Đorđe P</span></a></li><li class="meta-date" ><time class="ct-meta-element-date" datetime="2026-01-23T21:00:00+09:00">2026-01-23 21:00</time></li><li class="meta-comments"><a href="https://automaton-media.com/en/news/japanese-indie-game-in-which-you-use-your-stupid-little-hamster-as-a-war-weapon-of-mass-annihilation-launches-to-very-positive-score-on-steam/#comments">1 Comment</a></li></ul></article><article class="entry-card card-content post-5902 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-news tag-global-news tag-nintendo" ><ul class="entry-meta" data-type="simple:slash" data-id="meta_1" ><li class="meta-categories" data-type="simple"><a href="https://automaton-media.com/en/news/" rel="tag" class="ct-term-3">News</a></li></ul><h2 class="entry-title"><a href="https://automaton-media.com/en/news/20211110-5902/" rel="bookmark">Animal Crossing: New Horizons’ The Roost is filled with little side stories</a></h2><a class="ct-media-container boundless-image" href="https://automaton-media.com/en/news/20211110-5902/" aria-label="Animal Crossing: New Horizons’ The Roost is filled with little side stories"><img width="768" height="432" src="https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/20211106-181402-header-768x432.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/20211106-181402-header-768x432.jpg 768w, https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/20211106-181402-header-600x338.jpg 600w, https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/20211106-181402-header-380x214.jpg 380w, https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/20211106-181402-header-150x84.jpg 150w, https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/20211106-181402-header-300x169.jpg 300w, https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/20211106-181402-header-696x392.jpg 696w, https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/20211106-181402-header-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/20211106-181402-header-747x420.jpg 747w, https://automaton-media.com/en/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/20211106-181402-header.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" style="aspect-ratio: 4/3;" /></a><div class="entry-excerpt"><p>Animal Crossing: New Horizons’ The Roost is filled with little side stories. A certain popular character has made a career change.</p>
